\title{In-place interfaces}
\meta{toc}{false}

\p{These objects update in place. In particular, \code{optimizer.ask(N)} returns points directly and \code{optimizer.tell(x, y)} returns fitted means. The [functional interface](docs.html) returns a new state alongside its result.}

\<section>[id]{baux.create_optimizer}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.create_optimizer}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.create_optimizer}](api-objects.html#baux.create_optimizer)}}
  \pre{
baux.create_optimizer(*, bounds: np.ndarray, config: OptimizerConfig, rng: Generator) -> Optimizer
  }
  \p{Create an optimizer that updates in place.}
  \p{All arguments are keyword-only. \code{bounds}: \code{(D, 2)} array. \code{config}: an \code{OptimizerConfig}. \code{rng}: a NumPy random generator. Returns \code{Optimizer}.}
  \p{Use \code{baux.chain(...)} to compile transforms before passing them as \code{config}. For structured parameters and explicit state transitions, use \code{baux.init}.}
  \<div>[class]{api-example}{\<p>[class]{example-label}{Example}
\pre{
import numpy as np
import baux

bounds = np.array([[-1.0, 1.0], [-2.0, 2.0]])
cfg = (baux.enn(k=5) | baux.ucb(beta=1.5))()
rng = np.random.default_rng(0)
opt = baux.create_optimizer(bounds=bounds, config=cfg, rng=rng)
x = opt.ask(num_arms=3)
y = np.sum(x**2, axis=-1, keepdims=True)
pred = opt.tell(x, y)
telem = opt.telemetry()

assert x.shape == (3, 2)
assert pred.shape == (3, 1)
assert isinstance(telem, baux.Telemetry)
}
  }
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/bo.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/bo.py#L356)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.Optimizer}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.Optimizer}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.Optimizer}](api-objects.html#baux.Optimizer)}}
  \pre{
baux.Optimizer(d: int, rng: Generator, inner: Any, *, identified_asks: bool = False)
  }
  \p{An in-place ask/tell optimizer.}
  \p{Construct with \code{create_optimizer}. \code{ask(N)} returns a coordinate matrix; \code{ask_batch(N)} returns an \code{AskBatch} with typed regional tickets.}
  \p{\code{tell(x, y, y_var=None)} records a batch and returns fitted means. \code{complete(ids, y, y_var=None)} and \code{cancel(ids)} update regional tickets in place and return \code{None}. \code{restart_region(slot, center)} returns abandoned tickets.}
  \p{\code{import_observations(x, y, y_var=None)} adds external data. \code{posterior_mu(x)} predicts without ingestion. Properties include \code{num_observations}, \code{num_regions}, \code{tr_length}, \code{init_progress} and \code{pending_ids}. \code{telemetry()} returns phase timings.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/bo.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/bo.py#L157)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.ENN}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.ENN}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.enn}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.ENN}](api-objects.html#baux.ENN)}}
  \pre{
baux.ENN(
    train_x: np.ndarray,
    train_y: np.ndarray,
    train_yvar: np.ndarray | None = None,
    *,
    scale_x: bool = False,
    index_driver: NeighborIndex = NeighborIndex.FLAT,
    work_dir: str | os.PathLike[str] | None = None,
    enn_storage: str | None = None,
    y_bounds: np.ndarray | None = None,
    **options: Any,
)
  }
  \p{A mutable ENN dataset and prediction model.}
  \p{\code{train_x}: \code{(N, D)}. \code{train_y} and optional \code{train_yvar}: \code{(N, M)}. Unlike \code{enn_init}, this constructor requires two-dimensional output arrays.}
  \p{\code{index_driver} selects the backend. Extra options include \code{device}, \code{index}, \code{storage}, \code{metric_learning}, \code{geometry} and \code{local_k}. \code{y_bounds} supplies \code{(M, 2)} output bounds.}
  \p{\code{add(x, y, yvar=None)} appends in place. \code{posterior(x, params, flags=...)} returns moments; \code{posterior_draw(x, params, function_seeds=..., flags=...)} returns draws and neighbor IDs.}
  \p{NumPy queries return \code{ENNNormal}. Supported device queries return a native \code{Posterior}. The presence of a device argument does not imply every operation runs there; inspect \code{capabilities}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/enn/enn_class.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/enn/enn_class.py#L186)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.ENNFitter}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.ENNFitter}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.enn}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.ENNFitter}](api-objects.html#baux.ENNFitter)}}
  \pre{
baux.ENNFitter(k: int, rng: Generator, *, infer_aleatoric_variance_scale: bool = True)
  }
  \p{Track fitting statistics for a mutable ENN model.}
  \p{\code{k}: neighbor count. \code{rng}: NumPy generator. \code{infer_aleatoric_variance_scale}: whether to fit the aleatoric scale.}
  \p{Call \code{tell(x, y, yvar)} to update statistics, then \code{ask(model, num_candidates=..., num_samples=...)} to get \code{ENNParams}. For the functional equivalent, use \code{enn_fit}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/enn/enn_fitter.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/enn/enn_fitter.py#L19)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.Telemetry}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.Telemetry}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.turbo.optimizer_types}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.Telemetry}](api-objects.html#baux.Telemetry)}}
  \pre{
baux.Telemetry(
    dt_fit: float,
    dt_sel: float,
    dt_gen: float = 0.0,
    dt_tell: float = 0.0,
    num_candidates: int = 0,
)
  }
  \p{Timings and candidate count from optimizer work.}
  \p{\code{dt_fit}, \code{dt_sel}, \code{dt_gen} and \code{dt_tell} are durations in seconds. \code{num_candidates} is the candidate count. Available as \code{state.telemetry} or \code{optimizer.telemetry()}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/turbo/optimizer_types.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/turbo/optimizer_types.py#L26)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.TellPredictionError}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.TellPredictionError}[data-kind]{class}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.TellPredictionError}](api-objects.html#baux.TellPredictionError)}}
  \pre{
class baux.TellPredictionError(RuntimeError)
  }
  \p{Ingestion succeeded but retrieving predictions failed.}
  \p{A \code{RuntimeError} subclass with \code{observations_accepted=True}. In the in-place optimizer, retry \code{optimizer.posterior_mu(x)} rather than submitting the same observations again. This exception does not classify errors from ingestion itself.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{python/baux/bo.py}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/python/baux/bo.py#L94)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.enn_optimizer}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.enn_optimizer}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.enn_optimizer}](api-objects.html#baux.enn_optimizer)}}
  \pre{
baux.enn_optimizer(bounds, k = 10, num_init = 10, seed = None, config = None)
  }
  \p{Construct the native ENN optimizer handle.}
  \p{\code{bounds}: \code{(D, 2)} array; \code{k}: neighbor count; \code{num_init}: initialization budget. Returns a native optimizer handle. \code{config} uses the native configuration representation.}
  \p{For Python configuration records and functional state, use \code{init}; for the in-place Python wrapper, use \code{create_optimizer}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{rust/crates/baux-py/src/py_optimizer/build.rs}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/rust/crates/baux-py/src/py_optimizer/build.rs)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.create_zero}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.create_zero}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.create_zero}](api-objects.html#baux.create_zero)}}
  \pre{
baux.create_zero(bounds, num_init = 10, seed = None, config = None)
  }
  \p{Construct the native surrogate-free optimizer handle.}
  \p{\code{bounds}: \code{(D, 2)} array; \code{num_init}: initialization budget. Returns a native handle. \code{config} uses the native representation. The Python configuration preset is \code{turbo_zero}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{rust/crates/baux-py/src/py_optimizer/build.rs}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/rust/crates/baux-py/src/py_optimizer/build.rs)}
}

\<section>[id]{baux.create_lhd}[class]{api-entry}[data-symbol]{baux.create_lhd}[data-kind]{function}[data-module]{baux.bo}{
  \<div>[class]{api-entry-header}{\<h2>[class]{api-entry-title}{[\code{baux.create_lhd}](api-objects.html#baux.create_lhd)}}
  \pre{
baux.create_lhd(bounds, num_init = 10, seed = None, config = None)
  }
  \p{Construct the native LHD optimizer handle.}
  \p{\code{bounds}: \code{(D, 2)} array; \code{num_init}: initialization budget. Returns a native handle. \code{config} uses the native representation. The Python configuration preset is \code{lhd_only}.}
  \<p>[class]{api-source}{[Source in \code{rust/crates/baux-py/src/py_optimizer/build.rs}](https://github.com/Kvutza/baux/blob/main/rust/crates/baux-py/src/py_optimizer/build.rs)}
}
